-Legacy consumed tombstones contain no owner address. Unexpired tombstones
-require authoritative ownership evidence or migration refuses atomically;
-permanent consumed tombstones cannot be resolved merely by waiting. A retained
-row proves an owner only when its caller key and original expiry generation
-match exactly. Multiple candidates require a mapping selecting one candidate.
-Existing results, original expiry, consumed fences, queue identity and ordering
-are preserved. Expired ownerless fences remain legacy provenance rather than
-being assigned an invented tenant.
-
-Resolved-owner provenance remains independent of active fences: replaying a
-recorded mapping validates it without resetting TTL or resurrecting an evicted
-fence. Stop old readers/writers before conversion. Old PG mutation SQL is
-rejected at the database boundary; the old redb open protocol rejects schema 2.
-Rollback requires the untouched pre-upgrade backup with new writers stopped;
-it does not recover subsequent new writes. Configuration builders do not
-collect owner evidence or convert schema-1 embedded files automatically.
